it9308 bundles two things that are not original work:

1. `it9308/firmware.bin` — the IT930x bridge firmware image, extracted from the
   vendor Android application. It is vendor firmware, not covered by this
   project's MIT licence. It is kept for private interoperability testing only;
   do not redistribute it. The driver cannot start a blank bridge without it;
   `list` and the tests do not need it.

2. `vendor/usb/` (pyusb, BSD-3-Clause) and
   `vendor/windows/x64/libusb-1.0.dll` (libusb, LGPL-2.1). Their licences are
   in `vendor/usb/LICENSE` and `vendor/windows/x64/LICENSE`.

`it9308/sequence.py` and `docs/9309-vendor-capture.txt` are protocol captures
(observed USB traffic), not firmware, and are part of this tree.

## Provenance marker

`it9308-pbcnx` is a visible provenance/attribution string in the Python and Java
metadata (`--version`, `It9308Device.PROVENANCE`). It is intended to make the
origin searchable and to encourage the MIT notice to travel with copies. It is
**not** telemetry: it performs no network or device I/O, carries no user or
device identifier, and changes no protocol bytes.
